      "text": "To find \\( x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} \\) given that \\( x - \\frac{1}{x} = 4 \\), we start by using the identity for the cube of a difference. The identity is:\n\n\\[\n\\left( x - \\frac{1}{x} \\right)^3 = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} - 3 \\left( x - \\frac{1}{x} \\right)\n\\]\n\nWe know from the problem statement that \\( x - \\frac{1}{x} = 4 \\). Substituting this value into the identity, we get:\n\n\\[\n4^3 = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} - 3 \\cdot 4\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the left side and the right side, we have:\n\n\\[\n64 = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} - 12\n\\]\n\nTo isolate \\( x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} \\), we add 12 to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[\n64 + 12 = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n76 = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} \\) is \\(\\boxed{76}\\).",
